## Diagnosis

The gate's `ok: false` was caused by exactly one file — `release/ProbeScratch.lean` (exit 1), the leftover API-discovery probe from checkpoint 1 (a scratch `#check` file; not a test or negative control, which live outside `release/`). Twelve of its `#check` lines referenced identifiers that don't exist at the pinned mathlib revision `7974e751bece493b6ff508039423ca9fa2452fa8`. The gate diagnostic was truncated at the top, so the full failure set was recovered by recompiling against the pinned-revision olean cache (which `lake build` had refreshed).

## Fix

Corrected all 12 identifier spellings, each verified against the pinned mathlib source:
- `MeasureTheory.integral_withDensity_eq_integral_smul{₀}` / `...setIntegral...` → bare root names (the lemmas are declared at the **root** namespace, after `end ContinuousLinearMap`, in `MeasureTheory/Integral/Bochner/ContinuousLinearMap.lean`)
- `continuous_det` → `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.continuous_det`; `Matrix.det_pos` → `Matrix.PosDef.eigenvalues_pos`
- `support` → `Function.support`; `Matrix.det_toLin'` → `LinearMap.det_toLin'`; `Matrix.nonsing_inv` → `Matrix.inv_def`; `Matrix.det_inv` → `Matrix.det_nonsing_inv`; `Matrix.dotProduct` → `dotProduct`; `Measurable.matrix_det` → documented as absent (measurability via `Continuous.matrix_det` + `Continuous.measurable`); `isCompact_tsupport` → documented as absent

**No theorem, definition, or D12 layer source changed** — every `Poincare/D12/VolumeIBP/*.lean` sha256 is identical to the previous checkpoint.

